Why This Is Asked
This question probes practical API-testing with event-driven, multi-tenant systems and guarantees like at-least-once delivery, idempotency, and DLQ routing.

Key Concepts
- Idempotency per tenant
- End-to-end delivery guarantees
- Failure modes: broker outage, consumer downtime
- Observability: audit logs and DLQs

Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo-test: ensure duplicate webhook does not double-process
async function testIdempotentWebhook(httpPost, tenantId, event){
  const first = await httpPost(`/tenants/${tenantId}/webhooks`, event)
  const dup = await httpPost(`/tenants/${tenantId}/webhooks`, event)
  assert(first.status === 200 && dup.status === 200)
  // verify idempotent side-effects only occurred once
}
```

